R-NI4 R-DL1 R-DL2 R-DL4 R-DL5 R-DL6 R-UP6 R-P3 R-P5 R-LF4 R-J3 R-HF1 R-NM8 (slice 039b, `tln upgrade roc` with the optional compiler downloads, U5): 16 runs on 16 projects. The command code is `PickOptional.step!` (called from `PickLoop.probe_round!`), `NightlyFlow.plan!` (the optional list), `InstallFlow.finish!` (`data.downloads`, the cap note). The pure part is `NightlyPlan.optional`, with `Consent.optional_*` of slice 037c.
The world: the compilers n08 (on PATH), h0, n10, n11, n12 and n14 (n14 is hidden by min-release-age, R-C7). H is h0, the pin of all headers. N is n12. The optional compilers are n11 and n10 (allowed, not older than H, not installed, not N, not H). Packages: ja fails on n12 only, jb fails on n12 and n11, jc passes on all (the fake units). `upgrade roc` holds the packages, so only the compiler moves.
The rule (the tested reading): the search asks an optional compiler only when a pair needs it (R-DL2: an optional download only widens a probe search, R-P5). With no opt-in the optional compilers leave the search with one line on stderr (R-DL4). The opt-in is `--probe-downloads` or `--yes`: the compiler is downloaded when a pair needs it, inside the cap `probe.max-toolchains` (R-DL6) and inside the budget `probe.max` (R-P5). `--allow-downloads` and `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL` do not answer an optional download (R-DL5). The prompt of the run asks for the required downloads only (N, H): never for an optional one (U5 reading (c)).
Run 1 (CI, no opt-in, only H installed): N is the one required download (R-UP6: it starts with no person). ja fails on n12, so the search needs n11, which is optional and not installed: one line `skipped 2 compiler downloads (148.1 MB), pass --probe-downloads` (n11 and n10, the compilers that leave the search). The result is H: `nothing to change`. No prompt, no `tty` call.
Run 2 (CI, `--probe-downloads`): the same, but n11 is downloaded (the answer line, no prompt), probed (a pass) and chosen. The pin moves to n11, not to N. The ladder runs on n11 (check and build pass).
Run 3 (`--yes`, a person, n10 installed): `--yes` is the opt-in (R-DL5, R-NM8): N and n11 are downloaded with no prompt. n10 is installed, so it is no download.
Run 4 (CI, `--allow-downloads` and `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes`): neither opts in (R-DL5). The line of run 1, `nothing to change`.
Run 5 (`probe.max-toolchains = 0`, `--probe-downloads`): the cap is 0: no offer (R-DL6). No line, no download, no note. `nothing to change`.
Run 6 (cap 1, `--probe-downloads`, jb fails on n12 and n11, the downloads work): n11 is downloaded and probed (a fail). n10 is wanted next, and the cap is spent: it is not downloaded. The note `probe.max-toolchains is 1 and 1 compiler download was not made. Set probe.max-toolchains higher.` The result is H.
Run 7 (cap 1, every download fails, ja): the download of n11 fails (a warning, no fact, the try counts for the cap, R-P3, R-DL6). n10 is wanted next: the cap is spent, so no `curl` call for it, and the note. The result is H.
Run 8 (default cap, every download fails, ja): n11 fails (the warning), n10 fails (the warning). Each is tried once: a failed compiler is not asked again. The result is H.
Run 9 (`--dry-run --probe-downloads`, a person): `--dry-run` answers No to optional downloads (R-LF4): the line of run 1, no download, nothing written. No prompt and no `tty` call (R-HF1).
Run 10 (`--json --probe-downloads`, CI): n11 is downloaded and chosen. `data.downloads` is 1 (the optional downloads count, as slice 025 Q7), `data.pinned` is n11.
Run 11 (U5, a person, no opt-in, H and N missing): ONE prompt, `Download 2 compilers, 148.1 MB: <N>, <H>? [Y/n]`: it names N and H only. The person says Enter. N and H are downloaded. ja fails on n12, the search needs n11: the line `skipped 2 compiler downloads` and no second prompt. The result is H (the pin stays).
Run 12 (U5, a person, `--probe-downloads`, H and N missing): the same prompt for N and H alone (one `tty` call, one `ask` call). After the answer, n11 is downloaded with the answer line and no second prompt. The pin moves to n11.
Run 13 (`probe.max = 2`, `--probe-downloads`): the 2 probes of the round on n12 (the platform and ja) use the budget. n11 is wanted, but no probe can start: no download (R-P5), no `curl` call. Exit 12 with the budget text.
Run 14 (`--probe-downloads`, jc passes on N): no optional compiler is needed, so none is downloaded and no line is printed (R-DL2). The pin moves to N.
Run 15 (CI, no opt-in, jc passes on N): the same with no line (the line shows only when the search needs a compiler that it cannot use).
Run 16 (`--probe-downloads`, jb): n11 is downloaded and fails, then n10 is downloaded and passes. 2 downloads, the pin moves to n10 (the newest compiler on which all held hashes pass).
